{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486364-setting-change-there-are-no-anarch-domains","id":1486364,"title":"[Setting Change] There are no Anarch Domains","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-13T14:47:12-07:00","id":1486364,"title":"[Setting Change] There are no Anarch Domains","content":"So, not wanting to derail either of the other Anarch domain related conversations, I had a thought about changing the Movement a bit that addresses certain things brought up in both of those thread:<br /> <br /> The Anarch Movement doesn't seek to establish Domains. That's why there's no idea of what an Anarch Domain looks like, or any uniformity to those that might qualify for that idea. The Anarch Movement simply seeks to establish local rule over Sect rule, where every local Domain's relationship with other Domains is a negotiated affair instead of part of some massive organization that robs local vampires of their power.<br /> <br /> The ideal &quot;Anarch&quot; Domain is actually an Independent Domain. Domains with no allegiances to anyone or any group outside their Domain unless they choose to; including any fidelity to the Anarch Movement if that's how things play out. Independent Domains that operate like Camarilla Domains but don't answer to the Camarilla are not a fail-state for the Anarchs as long as it's still self determined by the locals to work that way. The Free States being a thing is similarly within ideals because it's a mutually agreed upon alliance, not lasting is actually to the Movement's preference even if Independent Domains being taken over by Sects is not.<br /> <br /> As I see it, this offers the following benefits:<ul><li>Independent Domains are already the thing in the setting, and this expands their role as part of the bigger picture instead of largely being a fluke of authors wanting to make the Caribbean, southern Central American, and South American cities flavorful but without the knowledge base of how. STs are empowered to create quirky cities that operate on their own systems, with inherent conflict between the Anarchs that helped &quot;free them&quot; into this state and want to keep it that way, the Camarilla that doesn't want to lose their ability to send in powerful vampires to exert control, and the locals that don't want to bow to either.</li> <li>If you're using the V5 setting changes, this helps explain the draw of the Anarchs to the Ministry and Tzimisce: both are heavily related to regions known for Independent Domains; backing the Movement helps ensure many of their older holdings get to stay the way those Clans like things and less beholden to playing by the rules of a larger organization.</li> <li>There is inherent narrative conflict among the Anarch Movement on how interventionist to be. Factions are inherently going to form over whether the Anarchs should come in uninvited, and how long they should stay after any Sect loyal opposition is dealt with under the idea of making sure the new local government is up and running. This also provides a lot of places to explore some real world debates around different types of libertarianism and anarchism that makes the OOC name &quot;Anarch&quot; relate more to what they do IC, as well as other political topics like interventionism, colonialism, and so on.</li> <li>This also creates a narrative space for the Movement that gets them out of the &quot;but if they win they just turn into the Camarilla-lite&quot; issue. The Anarchs can be anywhere, and everywhere, because winning for them isn't about being a &quot;proper&quot; Sect but about fundamentally challenging the validity of having Sects in the first place. The Anarchs don't consider things a win unless their efforts prove to the locals that they don't need anyone above them to run things properly for themselves. All but the most dedicated Princes and Bishops are going to be at least slightly tempted by the subversive idea that they could be the true top and not have to worry about a Justicar or Archbishop looking over their shoulder.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T15:03:35-07:00","id":1486365,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting idea, but eyed from a certain perspective, there is a bit of a feel of &quot;some Anarchs read the VtR books and proclaimed the world should work like that.&quot; Which, nothing wrong with that, it's just bemusing to look at from a &quot;the goal of the Anarch movement is to turn the VtM setting into the VtR setting.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T15:35:17-07:00","id":1486366,"title":"","content":"True, though VtR also just reflects VtM with a team with more experience in understanding macro-politics and how to construct a setting. The Carthians are also proof that even if the Anarchs somehow &quot;won&quot; and completely got rid of Sects, there would still be vampires unsatisfied with the new status quo and look for a way to channel that feeling with like-minded vampires.<br /> <br /> I think though, it avoids too much of the &quot;stealing from VtR&quot; aspect of things (even if that was a problem) because it's not bringing anything from VtR into VtM. There were vampires in VtM that wanted there to be no Sects long before I posted this, or VtR 1e was written... they just weren't the dominate ideology of any larger group.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T15:40:21-07:00","id":1486368,"title":"","content":"That's definitely a thing, and certainly there were characters and groups and the like in VtM that wanted a teardown of all the sects and what all have you. <br /> <br /> Really I wasn't being direly serious there, it was just funny considering the discourse on all the setting changes to look at it as &quot;this time for the Anarchs it's a specific in text goal!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T16:18:48-07:00","id":1486370,"title":"","content":"It does make me wonder how the Anarchs ever actually win territory? There's a reason why the dominate powers in the real world are large oligarchies with an organized, hierarchical army. Such nations can simply field bigger, more organized armies. The Anarchs should get crushed by the Sabbat or Camarilla. Almost literally run over by them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T16:45:05-07:00","id":1486373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486364-setting-change-there-are-no-anarch-domains?p=1486370#post1486370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does make me wonder how the Anarchs ever actually win territory? There's a reason why the dominate powers in the real world are large oligarchies with an organized, hierarchical army. Such nations can simply field bigger, more organized armies. The Anarchs should get crushed by the Sabbat or Camarilla. Almost literally run over by them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not just that, Large hierarchies are also much better at fielding disruption, propoganda, espionage, and economic warfare. Large, well-established systems are just better at pooling massive amounts of resources into a task and assigning people to that task.<br /> <br /> A domain-less Anarch state would be entirely reliant on crowd-funding and voluntary defence, which are historically horribly vulnerable to turning on each other from insider threats and mass Desertion by the weak-willed the moment members feel like<i> their</i> lives are in danger.<br /> <br /> Ironically, An anarch-state that didn't essentially become everything it hated would be too weak to defend against the things it hates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T16:56:10-07:00","id":1486375,"title":"","content":"Well, to the real world comparison: the big powers are generally too busy with each other. Sometimes big powers do just steamroll small powers (Tibet isn't a country any more), sometimes they setup proxy governments, but the Cold War ended with a lot of countries that aren't under the sway of any specific larger power because they weren't important enough for anyone to put in that effort by pulling away resources from more important battlegrounds. IRL there are currently ~20 countries (depending on how you want to define things) with no military... but nobody is rushing to conquer them. What major power thinks it's worth it to go take over Uruguay?<br /> <br /> Then there are, of course, lots of countries that are willing to make deals with the big powers to ensure neutrality. It's easier to have Switzerland take no sides than expend your forces to conquer Switzerland to make sure they don't side with your enemies. And the Swiss have spent a long time being happy to be that way.<br /> <br /> Or one can look at Afghanistan and it's long history of just being an epic pain in the ass to conquer.<br /> <br /> So yeah, there are avenues of claiming territory despite being a severe underdog on the global scale. Global power doesn't mean easily exerted power everywhere.<br /> <br /> The baseline setting of VtM is actually in the Independent Domains' favor. Vampire territorial expansion is hampered significantly by their small numbers, reliance on very long term planning, and need to wage proxy warfare. The Camarilla and Sabbat have enough trouble exerting military power over Domains a few miles away from their nearest powerful Domain, let alone hundreds of miles away. It was an intensely massive military campaign in Revised for the Sabbat in southern Florida to push the Camarilla out of Georgia, and the Carolinas, before the issues with the Regent led to Virginia being a stalemate.<br /> <br /> How are they going to manage to take over a city in Brazil from Mexico City? Or the Camarilla taking that city from Texas?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T19:03:13-07:00","id":1486381,"title":"","content":"Yes, this notion on big powers leaves aside a lot of nuance on how expansion and dominance really works. A good standing example of this is that this &quot;size&quot;-based thought led to the miscalculation that the war on Ukraine would exhaust their defenses and occupy Kyiv in two weeks tops. And for anyone wanting to argue &quot;there's a reason&quot;, that's exactly the point, even if this reason has to do with Ukraine having foreign support.<br /> <br /> Independent Domains wouldn't exist in a vacuum or try to, this is not the same as being independent. But they don't need to resist the entire might of sects. They need to resist the might those sects are capable of diverting to them specifically. And even then, context can change a lot of things as local powers, domestic politics and sect conflicts can drastically change the costs and consequences of claiming territory.<br /> <br /> For vampires, whose claim to dominance is even more based on insubstantial factors like secret influence instead of physical presence because they're so few in numbers, this is even more of a problem. How much harm can guerrilla warfare cause to a &quot;state&quot; whose stationed army is itself little more than a school gang in numbers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T00:16:08-07:00","id":1486392,"title":"","content":"This, and the approach of VtR, seem to be filled with Naivety.<br /> <br /> A government's method is stability; whether it's to make the government rich, make the country rich, or to simply stay alive, stability is key. Vampires cannot achieve stability with this kind of arrangement. Vampires need to control certain aspects of the city: nevermind an enemy, would you trust an ideological rival to hold the police force? The Camarilla, as a monopolistic but secular and fairly hands-off kind of government, is really a far-and-away better choice than a few colourful radicals agreeing to disagree.<br /> <br /> When you combine this with the realities of vampire living, IE everyone's a very dangerous individual, it'd be good for everyone's health if they ate Boss Kevin... yeah. Rules are good for everyone. Factions are one thing, but defined political parties are toxic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, this notion on big powers leaves aside a lot of nuance on how expansion and dominance really works. A good standing example of this is that this &quot;size&quot;-based thought led to the miscalculation that the war on Ukraine would exhaust their defenses and occupy Kyiv in two weeks tops. </div> </div> </div> This is more to do with the fact that common people have no idea how wars work. Anyone who was actually paying attention to such things knew that invading Ukraine would be a disaster for Russia. Like Chechnya, but bigger. Even if Russia took Kyiv, they'd have no way of actually holding onto things... and that's before we get into Russia's long list of other systemic issues.<br /> <br /> But to bring this back to topic: Vampire wars don't require the sprawling logistical feats of real, large scale wars. All the vampires in the WoD combined wouldn't match the population of a small European city. A conflict involving 50 vampires would be considered grand in scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T02:19:52-07:00","id":1486397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486364-setting-change-there-are-no-anarch-domains?p=1486392#post1486392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, and the approach of VtR, seem to be filled with Naivety.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is this any less true of the VtM political setup in general? The idea that the Camarilla and Sabbat could maintain the level of large scale control they do is nonsensical, and requires an incredibly surface understanding of politics to view as functional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A government's method is stability; whether it's to make the government rich, make the country rich, or to simply stay alive, stability is key. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the illusion of stability. But governments are inherently unstable because the world is unstable and governments have to adapt to the world as it changes. Populations don't desire stability, the desire predictability. Sometimes things are good, sometimes things are bad, and if a government tries to force things to always be even-keel human minds rebel because it goes against our fundamental psychological survival instincts. Back when complacency was a high risk of immediate survival failure (aka the vast majority of human history), our brains got wired to interpret neutral conditions as negative conditions so we wouldn't get lazy and overlook necessary tasks. There's a reason we have a gut reaction to overly positive developments as &quot;too good to be true,&quot; but overly negative ones with, &quot;it can get worse.&quot;<br /> <br /> A government structured around stability as its core tenet is doomed to rigidity and collapse. Governments need to be designed with a level of flexibility and adaptability because the world will demand it of them, and planned instability because the populace will create instability if there isn't any.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires cannot achieve stability with this kind of arrangement. </div> </div> </div>Vampires survived for thousands of years before any overarching Sects came into the picture, and as I noted from the outset there are Independent Domains in the setting as it is. So clearly they can.<br /> <br /> You seem to be misreading things based on the earlier back-and-forth regarding VtR: my idea is not that each city will have multiple Sects coexisting like Covenants do in VtR. Independent cities are Sect-less cities where power beyond the Prince/etc. isn't recognized as valid and local politics are matters of local vampires without the intrusion of figures from other continent and other centuries telling the vampires of tonight in a given location how things should be done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires need to control certain aspects of the city: </div> </div> </div>Given this is largely in the hands of Princes/Bishops/Barons/etc. as it is, and not something those above them manage directly, nothing at this level changes. The vampires of a city will control what they need to control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> would you trust an ideological rival to hold the police force? </div> </div> </div>Politics is about compromise. Your average Prince in your average Camarilla city has to deal with political rivals in positions of power as a default state of things. The only change in an Independent Domain is the the political and ideological conflicts are localized instead of federalized/globalized/etc. Different vampires having control and influence over different local institutions is inevitable as delegation becomes necessary, and this will inherently grow into political conflicts anyway.<br /> <br /> And yes, you'll take the devil you know over the one you don't. The ruler of an Independent Domain might want to run a &quot;secular&quot; society while a large portion of the local power players want official acknowledgement of the right to practice Paths, but that doesn't mean either side want the Sabbat rolling in to force their way of thinking on everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Camarilla, as a monopolistic but secular and fairly hands-off kind of government, is really a far-and-away better choice than a few colourful radicals agreeing to disagree. </div> </div> </div>Who said anything about the alternative to the Camarilla being radicals agreeing to disagree? If anything, that's the state as things are with how the Anarchs are written. The whole point of this change is to make so the Anarchs and the Camarilla are playing completely different political games, which creates the space for Domains to exist that bow to neither of them and run things on a more local level that's better able to handle the actual night-to-night business of keeping vampire society running.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is more to do with the fact that common people have no idea how wars work. Anyone who was actually paying attention to such things knew that invading Ukraine would be a disaster for Russia. </div> </div> </div>Plenty of experts assumed Russia would have done much better in the first few week of the war. They weren't expecting Russia to flat out conquer Ukraine without resistance, but take control over enough of the country and infrastructure to force Ukraine into accepting a really crappy peace deal for most of their country back; so Putin could have a much more friendly government in Kyiv again, or at least puppet autonomous regions controlling large parts of Ukraine that answer to him instead. As far as another outside the Kremlin can tell, that was the Russian plan: rush in and negotiate out before the quagmire sets in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But to bring this back to topic: Vampire wars don't require the sprawling logistical feats of real, large scale wars. All the vampires in the WoD combined wouldn't match the population of a small European city. A conflict involving 50 vampires would be considered grand in scale. </div> </div> </div>Which only supports the idea that Independent Domains are already viable in how the setting in constructed. The Camarilla trying to use force to keep cities from going Independent after Anarch infiltration and subversion efforts are successful would be a huge commitment of resources that is, ultimately, unsustainable compared to the using low resource efforts to destabilize the local Cam power structure and help friendly locals take it over for themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T06:22:41-07:00","id":1486407,"title":"","content":"1- Vampires can't effectively control people beyond the city state, and they have very little need to. While this supports the idea that Anarchs are fine, it really brings into question how overbearing is the Camarilla really? <br /> 2- Despite what I just said, Vampires DO have some need to expand influence beyond city limits. The Masquerade needs to be kept, trans-city criminals need to be caught, dangerous sects need to be quashed. Vampires might want or need to travel, but at the same time a prince allowing a new person to enter their city carries a level or risk. While it's perfectly possible for vampires to foster distant relations and rely on letters of recomendation, something like the Camarilla goes a long way in smoothing out issues. <br /> <br /> Without some kind of ideology, I think it'd actually be worse off to be in Anarch domains than Camarilla ones for neonates. Anarch domains in this context would naturally attract inhuman elders and crazy cults. The Camarilla really does a good job in softening the worse excesses of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T08:45:41-07:00","id":1486422,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> <br /> <br /> \u200b1 - Am I seriously reading someone say that defined political parties are toxic to state stability? Because individuals are dangerous? Do you have any idea of how many <i>relatively</i> stable countries have multi-party systems?<br /> <br /> 2 - Even then, this is not the VtR approach to begin with. The Covenants aren't mandated political parties to be around on every single city. What VtR does mostly is to recognize that super-powerful organizations spanning the globe with control over most cities, from the perspective of an inherently insular race, nonetheless, is stupid. Not because it isn't good management, but because it wouldn't be able to sustain itself against, you know, insularity and internal strife. From this, people coming up with organizations around the world is a given.<br /> <br /> 3 - Governments have a <b><i>goal</i></b> of stability. That's a far shot from achieving it. And the most stable ones are dynamic systems built to run with political dispute without breaking, like for example every single functional democracy on the world, even when they're only barely functional (and when we consider just barely functional, there's a lot of them). Those who try for single party, autocratic stability have to devote a <b>lot</b> of resources just to quash opposition <i><u>constantly</u></i>.<br /> <br /> 4 - You know what's inherently more stable? Focusing on local domestic politics and keep international politics as secondary. You know what's easier to keep stable, run and protect even against outside aggression? A small territory that makes allegiances and treaties with others instead of trying to conquer and control them directly. You know the best way to make far-reaching accords work? Base them on non-aggression first instead of on fighting a common enemy, which makes only for a temporary alliance with growing internal strife. You know who agrees with me on this? Roughly 180 countries on the real world, plus most international alliances and conventions, including the UN and NATO (a military alliance built around non-aggression that is currently desperately trying to <b>not</b> go to war with Russia).<br /> <br /> 5 - I also thought invading Ukraine would end badly. But guess what, a lot of <b>actual specialists, including military personnel</b> thought it could happen and wouldn't be the mess it became. Maybe not all of them agreed with the Russian state advisors on how quick and effortless it would be, but even those are, you know, actual specialists regardless of any failure. But it goes again on what I said: that's exactly the fucking point.<br /> <br /> 6 - Lesser armies versus lesser armies does not equate with greater ease on establishing global power. Even today small armies with guerrilla tactics stick to small territories, and that was true even when they didn't had more powerful neighbors. Militarily speaking, vampires are tribal at best.<br /> <br /> 7 - Vampires don't need big influence outside their cities for any of the reasons given, because most of those are things that, once outside your city, probably aren't your problem anymore. And if they are, communication with your neighbors does a good enough job.<br /> <br /> 8 - The Masquerade is a joke. It is a game convention. It is unfeasible one way or another. A world where breaches don't grow because people don't care doesn't works less than a world where a global secret government works tirelessly to snuff every breach because none should work by rl standards anyway. Yet VtR approach requires less pieces to work in this sense, so Disbelief Occam's Razor applies.<br /> <br /> 9 - Really, I'm growing extremely tired of your attitude of always presuming everyone else is an idiot. We're not all couch sociologists. <b>You</b> are, by your own words. You don't need to believe anyone in particular is an expert, but you should know there are actual experts in several humanities fields that play this game and potentially write on those forums, and there's always the possibility that someone bringing something up may actually know what they're talking about. Keep that in mind before smuggling saying things you're actually just defending because for whatever reason you decided to come to a thread about Anarchs to defend the Camarilla as the only thing that makes sense for two entirely distinct Vampire games with 7 editions combined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T10:06:45-07:00","id":1486438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486364-setting-change-there-are-no-anarch-domains?p=1486370#post1486370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does make me wonder how the Anarchs ever actually win territory? There's a reason why the dominate powers in the real world are large oligarchies with an organized, hierarchical army. Such nations can simply field bigger, more organized armies. The Anarchs should get crushed by the Sabbat or Camarilla. Almost literally run over by them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on what you think the Anarchs are as they're a loose coalition of many competing idealogies. I always liked the Brujah Council as an Anarch group that succeeded beyond anyone's wildest dreams and promptly became a competing sect to the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Just an incredibly totalitarian one with global ambitions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T10:19:38-07:00","id":1486441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486364-setting-change-there-are-no-anarch-domains?p=1486407#post1486407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Vampires can't effectively control people beyond the city state, and they have very little need to. While this supports the idea that Anarchs are fine, it really brings into question how overbearing is the Camarilla really?</div> </div> </div> </div>How it &quot;really&quot; is, isn't as relevant to how it seems to be when it comes to things like trying to convince vampires to not align with it. There's also, as noted, multiple editions with various levels of overbearing presented.<br /> <br /> If the Camarilla had perfect PR and management, the Anarchs wouldn't exist period.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite what I just said, Vampires DO have some need to expand influence beyond city limits. </div> </div> </div>This is addressed in the opening post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Without some kind of ideology, I think it'd actually be worse off to be in Anarch domains than Camarilla ones for neonates. Anarch domains in this context would naturally attract inhuman elders and crazy cults. The Camarilla really does a good job in softening the worse excesses of vampires. </div> </div> </div>What I don't think you seem to be appreciating:<br /> <br /> 1) The title of this thread is literal. In this setup there <b>are no Anarch Domains</b>. The Anarchs work to establish Independent Domains, who then operate however they want even if it's not how the Anarchs that &quot;liberated&quot; them would have liked.<br /> <br /> 2) It isn't meant to create a &quot;perfect&quot; situation. The whole point is that it makes Anarchs a different play experience from the Camarilla. Instead of playing in an Anarch Domain as they're currently handled by the games - that is you're basically playing the Camarilla but will less rules - it creates spaces for new game styles: from Movement specialists that go into a fragile Domain to push it to go Independent and help keep Independent Domains from sliding back to the Camarilla or Sabbat, to normalizing the option of playing Independent Domains where the problems that you're talking about are things to actually build stories about (Power mad elder thinks they can steam roll the weaker younger vampires and take the city over since it can't call on the Cam sounds like a good story to me).<br /> <br /> Basically, while there needs to be some level of attention played to suspension of disbelief here, and thus addressing some level of practical function, this is about expanding what the Anarchs can be about as PCs by freeing them from the restrictions that being a &quot;Sect&quot; entails; which tend to lead to the aforementioned &quot;Camarilla-lite&quot; playstyle problem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T10:24:06-07:00","id":1486442,"title":"","content":"Anarchs don't win fiefdoms in general as they are collection of younger and weaker kindred who don't like answering to monstrous elders and methsulaths who have a habit of killing or blood bonding people who will upset the apple cart. Other then that they don't have a unifying goal of what a new vampire society should be.<br /> <br /> In the words of my Brujah anarch &quot; If the Sabbat ever falls towards the Camarilla. We will be next on the list and I'm not sure we could mount of a meaningful defense.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T11:33:45-07:00","id":1486452,"title":"","content":"There's a decent number of established older and powerful Anarchs in the books... which doesn't really follow the idea that they're screwed because they're just too young and weak to accomplish much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T13:58:56-07:00","id":1486462,"title":"","content":"This thread has inspired me to get shitfaced and type up a post on the failings of the Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T14:21:28-07:00","id":1486463,"title":"","content":"Sounds like Seattle's Pioneers in VTMB2 and I was rather interested to see what they were like. Still, couldn't we have Anarchs <i>and</i> independents? Even if the independents outnumber the Anarchs and they overlap?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T14:43:45-07:00","id":1486464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486364-setting-change-there-are-no-anarch-domains?p=1486442#post1486442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anarchs don't win fiefdoms in general as they are collection of younger and weaker kindred who don't like answering to monstrous elders and methsulaths who have a habit of killing or blood bonding people who will upset the apple cart. Other then that they don't have a unifying goal of what a new vampire society should be.<br /> <br /> In the words of my Brujah anarch &quot; If the Sabbat ever falls towards the Camarilla. We will be next on the list and I'm not sure we could mount of a meaningful defense.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue against this actually because of the matter of perspective.<br /> <br /> For the majority of Methusalehs and ancient vampires like Mithras or even Lucian of Gary, the Camarilla is something of a joke and more or less the equivalent of a bunch of Kindred AOCs and Far Lefters having gotten together to talk about &quot;rights&quot; and &quot;privileges&quot; while they find the entire concept ridiculous. The Anarchs view the Camarilla as an ancient powerful institution but as Kindred reckon thing (at least prior to the Beckoning), it is a fairly new institution that is younger than the Anarch Movement itself. PRINCES are things that ancients understand because it is a thing that has existed back to Enoch and they understand the TRADITIONS but the actual politics-politics of vampiredom is something that pays no attention to the Inner Council.<br /> <br /> Chicago by Night 1st Edition illustrated that the Anarchs and Camarilla are two sides of the same coin to the Methusaleh because both of their sects are ireelevant to who REALLY controls the Jyhad. In punk terminology, one side may preach equality and the other side may preach order but at the end, they all answer to Menele or Helena.<br /> <br /> OPP should detail <b>Washington DC by Night</b> because that's the premise for Lucius Sejanus. After being rejected by the Camarilla and Sabbat, he just made himself ruler of an Anarch domain and all of the Anarchs joined with him because he probably paid them extremely well in Domain, blood, and cash.<br /> <br /> It's not like Sejanus is unfamiliar with Emperors being officially first among equals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T14:45:32-07:00","id":1486465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486364-setting-change-there-are-no-anarch-domains?p=1486463#post1486463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like Seattle's Pioneers in VTMB2 and I was rather interested to see what they were like. Still, couldn't we have Anarchs <i>and</i> independents? Even if the independents outnumber the Anarchs and they overlap?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you define Independents. Are they Clan based Independents, Autarkis who move from city to city like Beckett, or people who just want to keep their head down?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T15:52:00-07:00","id":1486471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486364-setting-change-there-are-no-anarch-domains?p=1486465#post1486465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on how you define Independents. Are they Clan based Independents, Autarkis who move from city to city like Beckett, or people who just want to keep their head down?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean kindred who want their community (usually meaning the city) to be outside the sects, regardless of how it's run. I think that's what Heavy Arms is describing. This could include:<ul><li>Medieval princes, and their successors, who rejected the Camarilla when it was created.</li> <li>Medieval princes, and their successors, who rejected the Ashirra when it was created. I note these guys separately, because it would have started earlier and <i>Playing the Sabbat</i> implied that Tzimisce in Anatolia and North Africa did this.</li> <li>Other princes who rejected any sect when they reached their part of the world, usually in Africa and Asia.</li> <li>Kindred of clans traditionally excluded from the sects, who control their own domain, usually Giovanni or Ministry.</li> <li>Kindred who settled in places beyond the grasp of sect authorities and maintained local autonomy (e.g. the Pioneers and I think some places in 2nd Edition/Revised South America).</li> <li>Kindred who overthrew sect authorities in their own domain and don't keep affiliation to any global sect. This includes:<ul><li>Anarchs who distrust organisation at larger scales.</li> <li>Kindred who approve of Camarilla (or even Sabbat) traditions, but not oversight from justicars or archons (or cardinals etc.)</li> <li>Princes who want to be sovereigns and subjects who think that benefits them for some reason.</li> </ul></li> <li>Kindred who are so isolated by circumstance rather than choice that the sect to which they nominally belong can't stretch far enough to intervene there and doesn't know what they're doing.</li> <li>Imitations of VtR cities. I've been trying to work out the San Francisco Mission and Swansea's traditionally Longinian, clan divided cloister, but they don't make much sense with VtM's history.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T16:09:32-07:00","id":1486472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486364-setting-change-there-are-no-anarch-domains?p=1486463#post1486463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, couldn't we have Anarchs <i>and</i> independents? Even if the independents outnumber the Anarchs and they overlap?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the idea. The Anarchs and Indepedent Domains would not be the same institutions. The Anarachs are a <i>Movement</i> that seeks to expand and support Independent Domains, which have always been a thing in the setting even if they fell out of fashion with the rise of the Camarilla and Sabbat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T03:14:18-07:00","id":1492582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486364-setting-change-there-are-no-anarch-domains?p=1486452#post1486452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a decent number of established older and powerful Anarchs in the books... which doesn't really follow the idea that they're screwed because they're just too young and weak to accomplish much.</div> </div> </div> </div>All sects have those. The Anarchs just seem to rely on plot armor much more than the Camarilla and the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T06:12:27-07:00","id":1492591,"title":"","content":"This is mostly how i run them so I wish I could smack the like button harder<br /> <br /> And for the reason why the camarilla doesn\u00b4t conquer all of them is because canonically the camarilla army is actually small and made of<ul><li>Justicars</li> <li>Archons</li> <li>Ghouls</li> </ul><br /> For example the camarilla presence in Chicago which is one of the most important domains amounts to three archons and a bunch of ghouls.<br /> <br /> The bulk of their force are local vampires joinning them as <u>&quot;reinforcement&quot;</u> and most of their warriors are actually neonates forced to fight by the blood bond under the flag of an archon labeled as Dux Bellorum. The other part of camarilla defenders are ancilla who are in a priviledged position but because they are priviledged they would rarely risk their unlife when victory is unsure or at the first line.<br /> <br /> Invading for the camarilla requires them to gather their forces at one point leaving other strongholds without any defense or start a recruitment campaign for neonates and desesperate vampires willing to put their unlifes at risk for a piece of domain (LaCroix?) which takes times and does not guarantee a result against an united domain<br /> <br /> The camarilla instead expand by financing and giving support to revolutions against princes who refuse to join their federation because they don\u00b4t want an outsider telling them how to rule or giving privileges to someone he does not even known because of favours.<br /> <br /> Add to all this that because his size and corruption the camarilla spends a great deal of his energy fighting revolutions inside their own domains. Not to mention other supernaturals or the sabbat. The camarilla isn\u00b4t invencible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T07:31:48-07:00","id":1492596,"title":"","content":"Despite that in his specific case he wasn't expected to succeed, it would be just a bonus if he did, LaCroix probably represents well the main Camarilla tactic against Anarchs: politics, not arms. This will always be their default, war is a last resort. Instead, carve out a niche in the city where you can put someone to act as Prince and let them sway public opinion with time. Maybe you can bribe a local to come to your side and act this part.<br /> <br /> As long as you have the resources and skill to provide more safety and stability than the local powers, the city will fall in line in time. You are immortal, no need to rush things. If you can't surpass your enemies politically, then even trying to conquer this city is probably a bad move anyway, going to hurt more than it's worth.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla would only go to open war if the city is too strategically important in a global scale, or too belligerent for the usual strategy <b>and</b> there are Camarilla vampires with personal interest in taking power there by force for their own sake. That may happen if you have a nearby Camarilla city that's too crowded and a number of ambitious vampires frustrated with low prospects at local power.<br /> <br /> But those would be rare situations. Most of their wars are either defensive or preemptive against targets that really will attack if left unchecked until they amass enough resources. Even such wars are hard enough to organize in the Cam. And I doubt they have enough Archons at any given time to have one in every big Camarilla city. How many Archons does a Justicar controls regularly? Most of the time I doubt their total number reaches 100 world wide, while the number of cities with more than a million inhabitants exceeds 500, so the Cam could have easily up to 200 under them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T08:14:13-07:00","id":1492600,"title":"","content":"I can't help but to think of the Oradea League when reading through this thread. That's clearly a group of powerful kindred that have made their own minor sect to be independent from the rule of the Sabbat and Camarilla. I wouldn't call the Anarchs, at least in the way the word is used in Vampire but, are free in the sense of being their own domain.<br /> <br /> In the aspect that the Anarch Movement is breaking down the larger sects into smaller domains, it makes more sense to me. The original Anarch fought against elders like those of the Oradea League in order to be free of their domination. Now the new Anarchs are fighting against the Camarilla and Sabbat to make more localized states like those seen in the war of princes. It's funny to me but, the Anarch Movement in general should be about over reach and not allowing kindred autonomy so it would track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T11:48:31-07:00","id":1492613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gimmisky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486364-setting-change-there-are-no-anarch-domains?p=1492582#post1492582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All sects have those. The Anarchs just seem to rely on plot armor much more than the Camarilla and the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean in that post is that the Anarchs could rely less on plot armor because they have some very impressive members to justify how they handled certain things.<br /> <br /> One of the problems though, is that the books tend to present Elder Anarchs as disillusioned. They recognize that if they exercise they personal power they have, the end up becoming that which they hate (Smiling Jack and Nines both say as much in Bloodlines); they're not in it to kick out the old kings and take crowns for themselves. They want a different way of doing things.<br /> <br /> That's why this thread was titled as a setting change, not just a discussion of what's already in the books. All the higher powered Anarch NPCs in the books would make more sense because they'd have more purpose being part of a movement creating change, than as Elders moping about how they don't become Baron because that's just another name for Prince.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}